    {
      "text": "Warm 1 1/2 tablespoons olive oil and garlic-flavored olive oil together in a skillet over medium heat until fragrant, about 1 minute. Stir in onions and mushrooms; reduce heat to low, and cook until the mixture has softened and caramelized, with browning around the edges, 8 to 12 minutes, adding additional olive oil if needed to prevent sticking.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/v7F1_pfwWYEgISo-63kV3s5grnE=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/88587-easy-portobello-mushroom-saute-ddmfs-2063-4x3-step-02-3773a950915f4653927888f8cb6d5064.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/88587/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn off heat, drizzle with remaining 1 1/2 tablespoons olive oil, and season with salt and pepper. Sprinkle generously with Parmesan and Asiago cheeses.",
